{title: 482 - Father, Lead Me Day by Day}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #482 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 482}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Father, [Bm]lead [D]me [G]day [A]by [D]day, [D]Ev[A7]er [D]in [A]thine [Bm7]own [E7]sweet [A]way;
[D]Teach me [G]to [B]be [Em]pure [D]and [Em]tru[A7]e, [D]Show me [Em]what [G]I [D]ought [A7]to [D]do.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D][Bm][D]When [G][A]in [D][D]danger, [A7][D]make [A][Bm7]me [E7][A]brave;
[D][G]Make [B][Em]me [D][Em]know [A7][D]that [Em][G]Thou [D][A7]canst [D]save;
[D][Bm]Keep [D][G]me [A][D]safe [D][A7]by [D][A]Thy [Bm7][E7]dear [A]side;
[D][G][B]Let [Em][D]me [Em][A7]in [D][Em]Thy [G][D]love [A7][D]abide.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D][Bm][D]When [G][A][D]tempted [D][A7]to [D][A][Bm7]do [E7][A]wrong,
[D][G][B]Make [Em][D]me [Em][A7]steadfast, [D][Em]wise, [G][D]and [A7][D]strong;
[D][Bm][D]And [G][A]when [D][D]all [A7][D]alone [A][Bm7]I [E7][A]stand,
[D][G][B]Shield [Em][D]me [Em][A7]with [D][Em]Thy [G][D]mighty [A7][D]hand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D][Bm]May [D][G]I [A][D]do [D][A7]the [D][A]good [Bm7][E7]I [A]know,
[D][G][B]Be [Em][D][Em]Thy [A7][D]loving [Em][G][D]child [A7][D]below,
[D][Bm]Then [D][G]at [A][D]last [D][A7]go [D][A]home [Bm7][E7]to [A]Thee,
[D][G][B]Evermore [Em][D][Em]Thy [A7][D]child [Em][G][D]to [A7][D]be.
{end_of_verse}
